00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.480
Before Wikipedia, keeping an encyclopedia current meant mailing out updates.

67
00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:10.640
Even after the moon landing, Jimmy Wales recalls his family's encyclopedia, a useful contrast with the continuously updated reference tools we now take for granted.

68
00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.600
Did you buy it in the store or did did somebody like come to your house and sell it?

69
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.000
No, somebody came to the house, door to door.

70
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.560
Um when I was a baby, as the family legend goes, that uh somebody came to the house and sold it to my mother.

71
00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:26.160
And um every year they would send out an annual update.

72
00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:26.720
Yeah.

73
00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.920
For example, the article on the moon was updated when someone landed on the moon.

74
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:40.360
And so they they were all these stickers, and you would take the sticker out and you would go to look up M Moon and you would find the old article on the moon, and you put in a sticker saying there's an update.

75
00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.560
My mom and I would do that every year when the stickers came in.

76
00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.760
My first editing and encyclopedia.

